74" 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517310 1080 "E(t)=a(t)" 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517310 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517310 1083 #uuid "6356a13a-040d-5ec9-83bf-cd04457292a6" 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517311 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517307 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517311 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517311 1071 "A model records the mass of grain in a silo at time $t$, measured in hours after observations begin.\n\n- $E(t)$ - the mass of grain in a silo, in kilograms.\n\n- $a(t)$ - the positive rate at which that amount is decreasing, in kilograms per hour.\n\nWhat is the relationship between $E(t)$ and $a(t)$?" 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517311 1072 #uuid "6a01eb6f-a624-502a-a2a4-9a6dfc01e40c" 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517311 1074 "The function $E(t)$ gives the mass of grain in a silo after $t$ hours. Then,\n\n$$\nE'(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}E(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }E}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, $E'(t)$ gives the instantaneous rate of change of that amount. The amount is decreasing, so the derivative is the negative of the positive loss rate $a(t)$. Therefore, the relationship is $E'(t)=-a(t)$.\n\nThe change ratio denotes an instantaneous rate: the limit of change ratios as the time interval tends to zero." 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517312 1068 #edb/ref 17592186517314 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517312 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517312 1071 "A model records the mass of grain in a silo at time $t$, measured in hours after observations begin.\n\n- $E(t)$ - the mass of grain in a silo, in kilograms.\n\n- $A(t)$ - the positive rate at which the amount is added, in kilograms per hour.\n\n- $L(t)$ - the signed contribution of removal to the rate of change, in kilograms per hour; $L(t)<0$ when removal occurs.\n\nWhat is the relationship between the three functions above?" 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517312 1072 #uuid "73bef49f-6ef2-549c-9aa9-8a94dc95239f" 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517312 1074 "The function $E(t)$ gives the mass of grain in a silo after $t$ hours. Then,\n\n$$\nE'(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}E(t)}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{\\text{Change in }E}{\\text{Change in }t}.\n$$\n\nThus, $E'(t)$ gives the instantaneous rate at which the amount changes at time $t$.\n\nIn addition, $L(t)$ already includes the negative sign of removal. We add the two signed contributions at time $t$. That is,\n\n$$\nE'(t)=A(t)+L(t).\n$$\n\nThe change ratio denotes an instantaneous rate: the limit of change ratios as the time interval tends to zero." 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517313 1080 "{E}^{′}(t)=A(t)\\cdot L(t)" 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517313 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517313 1083 #uuid "87998396-55ff-5827-af6b-d5ac4de36581" 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517306 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517313 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517316 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517317 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517314 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517319 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517314 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517314 1077 "selection" 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517314 1078 #edb/ref 17592186517319 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517314 1079 #uuid "9c8a937b-cd32-53bf-804a-42a180317817" 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517315 1080 "{E}^{′}(t)=-a(t)" 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592186517315 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535564 17592186045443 true] [17592